id: ops-compatibility-reasons
title: Explain joint compatibility constraints with minimal reason chains
description: "Explain package, host and extension incompatibility from declared version constraints and supported capabilities. Acceptance: three incompatible pins report the exact conflict and compatible ranges; unknown metadata differs from incompatibility; every proposed command is a preview with no installs or configuration edits. Deliver typed SDK and CLI, bounded TOON/JSON, typed refusals and remedies, README and example, no-git and read-only public tracker evidence, model-based replay tests, and CI npm plus Bun release gates."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T10:32:02.370Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T11:06:37.843Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T10:33:17.117Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: ops status/outdated report individual versions; backend-capabilities.ts verifies list/get/schema support; diagnostic-witnesses.ts reduces declared sufficient facts without solving versions. Sibling starter/presets compatibility-floor tests check manifest admission only. Installed SDK authoring exports checkExtensionManifestCompatibility with the loader-shared inclusive bounds; reuse it for extension checks. This feature explains joint declared dependency ranges and capabilities, leaving actual admission authoritative in core. Explicit bounded metadata input only; no registry fetch, install, configuration edit, tracker mutation, journal, claim or outbox path is introduced. Model tests cover JSON/TOON/file replay and SDK state read-back on a non-git tracker; mutation/recovery/status-role requirements do not apply to this observational path."
  "2026-10-27T10:43:11.513Z",codex-agent,"Focused suite passes 7/7; new module coverage is 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Behavioral revert: remove only intersection satisfiability filtering while retaining Cartesian clauses; the three incompatible pins regression fails 0/1 (expected joint_range_conflict, got installed_pin_conflict). Restoring the implementation returns the test to green. Public main export validation: SDK complete list 160 items, canonical get 1, schema 11 types; 2 components and 2 declarations produce 1 compatible row, 0 incompatible/unknown; JSON 847 bytes, TOON 887 bytes; all read-only source bytes unchanged. Seeded model completed 500 sequences / 3000 operations with SDK read-back of native state and relationships."
  "2026-10-27T10:47:18.493Z",codex-agent,"Linked acceptance passes 7/7 through pm test with 2 workers. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings (321 declarations across 40 files), duplication (0 clones), and production audit (0 vulnerabilities) pass. Clean-home strict health passes; the ambient global pm-github installation uses a newer host and reports version skew under the older pinned CLI, which is not a package tracker defect. Native extension admission remains separate. Output rendering explicitly preserves nested arrays/nulls in TOON and JSON. Additional boundary corpus covers maximum safe version segments, inherited-object refusal, optional-field round trips and 500 exact inclusive/exclusive patch-boundary cases."
  "2026-10-27T10:52:26.916Z",codex-agent,"Final design uses lazy public authoring-export acquisition only for native manifest checks; no argv, executable lookup or symlink-based SDK resolution. A real unsupported Node loader configuration exercises the typed compatibility_sdk_unavailable refusal without SDK mocks. The three-pin packet measures 933 JSON / 1007 TOON bytes. Native metadata is included in packed SDK/CLI acceptance across all six requested launch modes. CI npm/Bun gates and final packed acceptance are pending at push; the feature has no install/configuration mutation path."
  "2026-10-27T11:00:32.422Z",codex-agent,"The final solver reuses parsed semver witnesses and checks feasibility before expanding alternatives; it stops minimum-cardinality search at the first valid witness. Final focused suite again passes 7/7 through pm test, including all 500 operation sequences and 500 exact boundary cases; fresh new-module coverage remains 100% in all four dimensions. Repeating the function-only behavioral revert still fails exactly 0/1. Packed acceptance now uses isolated current Bun 1.4.4, matching the CI setup, because the preinstalled Bun 1.3.5 routes global installs into the local graph. The global fixtures assert that project package metadata stays unchanged. No shared runtime or tool installation is modified."
  "2026-10-27T11:06:37.842Z",codex-agent,"Wide version unions now remain one exact conjunction when expansion would exceed 16 alternatives, preserving npm prerelease rules while keeping agent output bounded. The 256-combination fixture and wildcard case cover this form; final source coverage is 100/100/100/100 after the focused suite plus the supplemental strict-boundary run. Packed topology inspection found that core directory snapshots from an external Bun global graph lose dependency discovery (missing toon dependency). The pinned host explicitly recommends its supported archive installer; global fixtures now use that core capability instead of rebuilding package resolution. This is a host activation UX limitation, not a missing SDK API or a product mutation path."
